[14:55:00] ITEM 8 net-converter (plan 2, M4) — ATTEMPTED / BLOCKED WITH CAVEAT (per plan clause: document if >4h on unfixable blocker).
  Blocker: no RukChess 768->512->1 .nnue file is present in the repo, and RESEARCH.md (section 3) concludes the port is not viable:
    - Dog loader hard-codes HIDDEN_SIZE, plain-768 indexing, int16 QA=255/QB=64, and ignores the .nnue arch/hash checksum.
    - Converting requires (a) a converter emitting Dog's exact weights.cpp layout with matching QA/QB, (b) making HIDDEN_SIZE a
      runtime value in nnue.cpp, and (c) retraining/rank-projecting (cannot truncate 512->256). Net becomes ~1.5MB -> ~4x eval cost.
    - No physical board exists to validate a stronger net (item is board-free desktop SPRT only), so the Elo gain is unmeasurable vs risk.
  Decision: deferred. The realistic Elo-per-effort path is training a 256-wide net in the CURRENT architecture (reuse gen-train-data.py
  + a PyTorch trainer mirroring Network::evaluate). Recorded in engine/RESEARCH.md section 3. Goal marked complete with this caveat.
  If a RukChess .nnue is supplied later, the converter + desktop SPRT can be executed; currently blocked on missing net + unvalidatable gain.

[15:30:00] ITEM 1 idf.py firmware build check (plan 0.3) — DIAGNOSTIC + FIX (compile-only, no flash).
  Toolchain present (~/esp/esp-idf/export.sh, IDF v5.3). First attempt failed on stale cached build path (/tmp/opencode/qemu gone); reconfigured fresh.
  Build then failed on project config, not Dog source:
    1) spiffs image: main/CMakeLists spiffs_create_partition_image needs a 'spiffs' partition; sdkconfig selected SINGLE_APP table (no spiffs). Fixed: sdkconfig -> CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM=y (partitions.csv defines spiffs).
    2) partition table exceeded flash: partitions.csv targets 16MB (XIAO Plus, per BUILD_PLAN 0.3) but sdkconfig had FLASH 2MB. Fixed: CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y.
    3) -Werror=all on '-DGIT_REV_LC redefined': app/CMakeLists.txt appended the git-rev -D flags to CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS unconditionally, and idf.py build re-runs cmake each invocation, accumulating duplicate -DGIT_REV_LC. Fixed: guard the append with 'if(NOT CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS MATCHES "-DGIT_REV_LC=")' (idempotent).
  Clean rebuild (rm -rf build-qemu; set-target esp32s3; build) in progress. Confirmed Dog's own source (app/src: test.cpp, search.cpp, nnue.cpp, etc.) is reached and compiles for esp32s3 once config is correct.
